{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40901-wraiths-as-minor-ish-template","id":40901,"title":"Wraiths as Minor(ish) Template?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T20:34:46-08:00","id":40901,"title":"Wraiths as Minor(ish) Template?","content":"I have some mechanical notes that I'm extremely uncertain on.<br /> <br /> I have to admit two things that are essential to deciding what's appropriate and what isn't appropriate for making this Minor Template: First, that I've read Geist but never played it, and while I'm very interested in it I don't have the sort of active experience with it that I have with other splats, so I need some help with it.<br /> <br /> Second, I didn't play Wraith and read a brief summary, and I'm less interested in emulating it and more interested in creating an interesting and fun way to play Ghost characters, with a lot of acknowledgement to Geist.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, here's a list of basic notes to describe it. Does any of it sound questionable to you guys? Do you think it's appropriate for Wraiths to have Keys &amp; Manifestations, for instance? How should they be reconciled with the GMC Ephemeral Being rules? Eager for your help to make something fun.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Wraith Mechanical Breakdown</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Overview</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Wraiths use mortal Attributes, <b>NOT </b>Spirit Attributes</li> <li>Wraiths utilize Ephemeral Being rules in God-Machine Chronicles</li> <li>Wraiths can also use Numina.</li> <li>Wraiths adopt aspects of the <b>Sin-Eater </b>template:<ul><li>Thresholds, Psyche, Plasm, Keys, etc.</li> </ul></li> <li>Wraiths use a modified Integrity as their Integrity Trait.</li> <li>Wraiths may have and purchase Physical and Mental Merits, but can be restricted in what Social Merits they can buy.</li> <li>Wraiths must consume Plasm in order to keep themselves from dissipating into the Underworld.</li> <li>Implied connection with Geists, perhaps step in transformation from Ghost to Geist?</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Attributes &amp; Skills</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Wraiths follow mortal character creation rules, retaining their attributes and skills they had in life. Their advantages are also the same.</li> <li>When they become Wraiths, ghosts regain the ability to adapt and change, and are once again able to purchase new attributes and skills, reflecting increased knowledge and a substantial alteration to their self-image.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Ephemeral Being Rules</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Wraiths <b>are </b>ephemeral ghosts and reside in Twilight by default.</li> <li>Wraiths use Plasm in place of Essence for all required upkeep. Wraiths must spend 1 Plasm every day to remain active. Wraiths that fail to pay their Plasm upkeep are banished to the Underworld.<ul><li>Wraiths can spend Plasm to boost their traits for a single scene on a point per dot basis, They can\u2019t boost a trait by any more than Psyche + 2 dots; boosting takes a turn and they may only boost a single trait in a turn.</li> </ul></li> <li>Wraiths are treat Rank with Psyche. (UNCERTAIN)</li> <li>Wraiths retain their Virtue and Vice as they had them in life. They are <b>not </b>reversed.</li> <li>Their Integrity is not fixed, it is slightly modified.</li> <li>Wraiths regain 1 Willpower per day.</li> <li>Wraiths retain their Influences and Manifestations. Additional Influences and Manifestations may be purchased. (UNCERTAIN)</li> <li>Wraiths are their own Anchors and are the subject of their Anchor Condition, unless their Integrity is reduced to zero, or they\u2019re sent to the Underworld. (UNCERTAIN)</li> <li>Wraiths keep their Banes but lose their Bans. (UNCERTAIN)</li> <li>Wraiths may purchase Numina.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Wraiths &amp; Sin-Eaters</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Wraiths share many similarities with Sin-Eaters.</li> <li>Wraiths have Thresholds. These affect their keys.</li> <li>Wraiths gain the Psyche and Plasm advantages.</li> <li>Wraiths have access to Keys. They begin play with the Two Keys of their Threshold, and may purchase others like Sin-Eaters.</li> <li>Wraiths have access to Manifestations when they have successfully Materialized. They begin play with three dots of Manifestations.</li> <li>Wraiths need Anchors and spend time in the Underworld based on Psyche?</li> <li>Wraiths regain Plasm through Haunts, Ectophagia, Threshold Resonance and Passions. (New Mechanic?)</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Integrity</span></span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Functions like normal with some breaking points removed and other universal breaking points added.</li> <li>Witnessing supernatural events is no longer a breaking point.</li> <li>Acting to gain Plasm confers a +2 bonus on breaking point rolls.</li> <li>Avoiding the living world for more than a week at a time is a breaking point with a zero negative modifier.</li> <li>Wraiths with Integrity Zero are banished into the Underworld and become Spectres, empowered but utterly beholden to the resonance of their threshold. Some say that Spectres go on to become Geists.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:13:06-08:00","id":41122,"title":"","content":"Two things to consider: the new Ghost Numina in <b>Mummy: the Curse</b>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40000-musings-on-a-new-wraith\">Musings on a new Wraith</a>. The former shoehorned a quick and dirty method of creating playable ghosts into the rules, and the latter explores themes and hypotheses regarding playable ghosts and considers some implications thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:31:14-08:00","id":41132,"title":"","content":"Both were inspirations for me, yeah. I just wanted to see what mechanics I could come up with. The use of full attributes should function like Lucid Dead, though I might revise some dice pools. Where I'm really unsure is just how to incorporate Geist mechanics, what is and isn't appropriate, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:27:09-08:00","id":41189,"title":"","content":"Going through them one by one:<br /> \u2022 Archetypes: \u201cyour archetype defines your relationship with and philosophy regarding death.\u201d Mechanically, it serves as a source of Plasm, in conjunction with Virtue and Vice. My own inclination would be to replace this with one or more Passions that likewise interact with Virtue and Vice to generate Plasm. IMHO, a key feature of the most interesting ghost stories is their driven pursuit of \u201cunfinished business\u201d. For a wraith, this choice should be emblematic of what draws him back to the land of the living. <br /> \u2022 Thresholds: mechanically, these determine which Keys a Sin-Eater starts out with. It\u2019s very logical that a ghost would have a Threshold. <br /> \u2022 Psyche: \u201ca Sin-Eater with a high Psyche is a deathly being, an expression of the afterlife in the mundane world.\u201d In addition to the standard features common to all power traits, sufficiently high Psyche grants a Sin-Eater one to three Anchors and demands that he periodically travel to the Underworld or lose Psyche. Frankly, I\u2019m not sure how appropriate either of these are for ghosts; at the very least, a wraith would need a modified version of Psyche. That said, it\u2019s worth noting that Unfettered Geists get a Psyche score. <br /> \u2022 Anchors: This means something different for Sin-Eaters than for ghosts: for a ghost, an anchor is something that tethers it to the mortal world and keeps it from being pulled into the Underworld; it also acts as a Condition for enabling the ghost\u2019s Manifestations \u2014 more on this below. More to the point, a ghost\u2019s Anchor is something in the material world that it can Influence. <br /> \u2022 Plasm: this is a physical substance out of which ghostly forms materialize. It\u2019s appropriate for Sin-Eaters, but not so much for ghosts. It\u2019s worth noting that both ghosts and unfettered geists are \u201cfueled\u201d by Essence. <br /> \u2022 Synergy: unless you\u2019re implementing an <b>Oblivion</b>-like split personality mechanic, this isn\u2019t appropriate for wraiths. <br /> \u2022 Keys: aspects of death that unlock portions of a Sin-Eater\u2019s Manifestations. It\u2019s worth noting that Keys work differently for Unfettered Geists, providing them with access to skills and letting them learn Numina based on Sin-Eater Manifestations. I\u2019d be more inclined to give wraiths suites of Key-based Numina that include, but are not limited to, Geist-style Key/Manifestation pairings. <br /> \u2022 Manifestations: for a Sin-Eater, these are powers of death unlocked by Keys: Boneyard, Caul, Curse, Marionette, Oracle, Rage, and Shroud. For GMC-style ghosts, Manifestations are ways to interact with the material world: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Avernian Gateway, Image, Materialize, Fetter, Unfetter, Possess, and Claim. The naming issue needs to be resolved, as these are two wildly different things. <br /> <br /> On the GMC side of things, ghosts have Rank, Essence, simplified attributes, Virtue, Vice, Integrity, Corpus, Willpower, Initiative, Defense, Speed, Size, Bans, Banes, Influence over Anchors, Manifestations, and Numina. As Ephemeral Beings, ghosts are subject to Summoning, Exorcism, Abjuration, Warding, and Binding. <br /> \u2022 Rank translates reasonably well to Psyche; note that Rank 1 ghosts are assumed to be drones. I\u2019d be inclined to say that Lucid Soul overrides this. Rank might benefit from being renamed. <br /> \u2022 Essence is fine as is, IMHO. <br /> \u2022 Agreed about using \u201cLucid Soul\u201d Attributes and Skills instead of the simplified Ephemeral Attributes. <br /> \u2022 Virtue and Vice are reasonable names to use. I think the inversion of Virtue and Vice should be treated as something specific to regular ghosts and spectres \u2014 in fact, the inversion of Virtue and Vice would be the primary defining distinction between Wraith and Spectre. <br /> \u2022 I don\u2019t think that wraiths should be defined by Integrity any more than vampires are. If you <i>do</i> decide to keep Integrity, don\u2019t ditch the \u201cexposure to the supernatural\u201d breaking points; but consider redefining what a ghost considers to be supernatural. <br /> \u2022 Bans and Banes are tied to Rank (or whatever it\u2019s called for wraiths). <br /> \u2022 Ghosts have an Influence rating equal to Rank that can be dedicated to one Anchor or split among several. The primary use for this is to establish the proper Conditions to Manifest; but at sufficiently high levels, the ghost can potentially do some very strange things. <br /> <br /> Some mechanism for determining which Manifestations a ghost has is needed. I\u2019d be inclined to assign dot ratings to each, based loosely on what prerequisites are needed to use them. Another source to look at here would be <b>Orpheus</b> \u2014 specifically, its Shades: Banshee, Haunter, Poltergeist, Skinrider, Wisp, etc. Each had a distinct personality type and a preferred means of manifesting; the former could provide a wraith\u2019s alternative to Archetype, while the latter could be adapted as a structure for Manifestations. <br /> <br /> Some system for assigning Numina is needed. My initial thought would be to make it Key-based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:39:08-08:00","id":41216,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at some of the systems presented in <b>Immortals </b>for inspiration here. I'll provide my write-up for Psyche to explain how I think it might apply to a Wraith. The chart I'm using would allow Psyche for Wraiths to be measured as a 1-5 point Power Stat which also alters the effective rank of a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel it worth mentioning that while Essence is good if it isn't well substantiated, I think Plasm is a good fit for Wraiths. For the one, it helps to further separate and make them distinct from the ephemeral ecosystem of the dead. I'm imagining Wraiths as very distinct aberrations from the rest of their Ghostly companions, which might lend itself to why they are their own Anchors, and why they have a certain physicality, allowing them to have their full traits and even physical merits. If Essence is the stuff of all ethereal beings, than Plasm might be seen as the very physical manifestation of that, and the Wraith's engagement with that very physical aspect of the world is enabled by their consumption of Plasm. Does that make sense as an explanation? If anybody has a finer understanding of Plasm, help me out so I know for certain whether this desire should be discarded.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the Integrity breaking points, that's a fair point, and while I do like the idea of keeping Integrity since Ghosts generally have it, I'll happily take any suggestions on an alternative. Since it isn't necessarily a &quot;major splat&quot; I was thinking it'd be better to keep Integrity to minimize any confusion.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">New Advantage: Psyche</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The psychology of a Wraith is a complex subject, as they attempt to adapt to housing a truly human mindset in the alien form of the ethereal dead. At first there\u2019s a disconnect between the Wraith and their existence as a ghost, but with time and contemplation, the Wraith is able to quell the dissonance within their own minds, accepting their state of undeath and the power that comes with it. Some enjoy a harmonious understanding of their nature and their mind while others wrestle a stronger connection, leveraging self over death. Regardless, this allows the Wraith to more easily channel the power of the Plasm which is an essential component of their being. With greater Psyche comes greater facility and power with Plasm, allowing the Wraith to store more of it in themselves and enhancing their abilities.</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #b7b7b7\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Psyche</span></b></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #b7b7b7\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Max Plasm/Max Plasm per Turn</span></b></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #b7b7b7\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Effective Ghost Rank</span></b></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">10/1</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">15/2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">16/3</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">17/4</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">20/5</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> </table></div> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-02-2014, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T16:38:57-08:00","id":41391,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?712791-nWoD-Musings-on-a-New-Wraith\" target=\"_blank\">rpg.net</a> thread had suggested Identity as the Integrity replacement, using the idea of the duality between mortal and post-life identities to represent 'Mask' and 'Dirge' (replacing Virtue and Vice). With that in mind I don't see a huge problem twisting things to make Synergy (as a mixture of those Identities) the morality stat. It regulates Identity to a theme rather than a game trait but that helps provide a sounding board for the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I was once a _______, but now I am dead. Who am I now?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This ties into Geist's theme of Second Chances but with a darker, sorrowful twist. It is too late for somethings and it is hard when you lose somebody. But when you lose everyone and everything are you still you? Do you fight your way back to make good your debts or look after your loved ones? Or do you move forward, with eyes on the future, leaving behind all you knew?<br /> <br /> Hindsight is said to be 20/20.<br /> <br /> The dead know this better than anyone.<br /> <br /> Plus, it means we have a method to bring back Spectures (in a VERY different shape) and a legit consequence for 0 Synergy: Your mortal and dead Identities are in total conflict. Some days you act as if you never died, not dissimilar from a blip. Some days you act as if you were never alive or even never born at all. And the other days you are insane, your mind and soul trying to reconcile these incompatible views of the world. Always, you fight to defend who you are.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, I think this works well with both the idea of Passions (from CWoD and M:tC) and Archetypes but since I'm not upto doing the mechanical side of things at the moment, I'll stick to fluff and concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:03:01-08:00","id":41404,"title":"","content":"These are some really excellent points, and I'm enjoying the additional mechanics. I'm just gonna admit I'm not sure I want to design them as a whole splat. Is it acceptable for them to have some of the mechanics of a full splat like that, if they're intended to be played alongside mortals/Sin-Eaters and whatever?<br /> <br /> Either way, I definitely dig that approach to the use of Synergy. At that point, it just begs the question of what mechanical systems should be used. Blood &amp; Smoke Humanity is a pretty likable model, I think. Maybe incorporating Banes as Compromises between the mortal and dead identities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T18:59:53-08:00","id":41451,"title":"","content":"I feel that Wraith has too much overlap with other groups in the nWoD for it to be an entire major splat, at this point at least. And since the threads working that project are in Geist, it makes sense to work from the perspective that Sineaters interact with them the most.<br /> <br /> I'd use them as a foil, to illustrate what the Bargin is and it's consequences. <i>&quot;There but for the grace of god I go,&quot;</i> is the sort of thing I'd like to have Sineaters and Wraiths think when they encounter each other, albeit with different emphasis.<br /> <br /> Besides, once we have the basics, we can work our way out from there when we're up to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:08:34-08:00","id":41499,"title":"","content":"I tend to view them as inversions of Sin-Eaters: where a Sin-Eater is a living person with one foot in the realm of the dead, a Wraith is a dead person with one foot in the land of the living. Where Sin-Eaters are focused on interacting with ghosts, Wraiths are focused on interacting with mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:16:44-08:00","id":41502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40901-wraiths-as-minor-ish-template?p=41499#post41499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to view them as inversions of Sin-Eaters: where a Sin-Eater is a living person with one foot in the realm of the dead, a Wraith is a dead person with one foot in the land of the living. Where Sin-Eaters are focused on interacting with ghosts, Wraiths are focused on interacting with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This elegantly sums up how I wanted to approach it. If I can draw some media comparisons, I kind of like the idea of a Wraith being a mixture of the ghosts in the first season of <i>American Horror Story </i>combined with Sally from <i>Being Human. </i>Sally in the free-roaming sense and the ghosts in AHS because they're really able to pull off the semblance to living beings, which I imagine Wraiths with their fuller self-image, ought to be much more capable of doing.<br /> <br /> So I have this goal, but I'm not sure what systems ought to be used to mechanically invoke it, what powers are necessary or unnecessary, etc.<br /> <br /> Part of my thinking now is that I'm not sure that they ought to use Keys &amp; Manifestations, because they feel like the inversion of the ghostly skillset, which is more about interacting with the living rather than the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:25:39-08:00","id":41669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40901-wraiths-as-minor-ish-template?p=41502#post41502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of my thinking now is that I'm not sure that they ought to use Keys &amp; Manifestations, because they feel like the inversion of the ghostly skillset, which is more about interacting with the living rather than the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they should use the same Keys, because those are tied to Thresholds, which ought to apply to wraiths. But different Manifestations, because enough of the powers would need to be altered (both for this interact with mortals point, and because of the corporeal vs incorporeal factor) that it would be easier to define new ones from scratch.<br /> <br /> (I do think they ought to be a major creature though).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:06:56-08:00","id":41804,"title":"","content":"I've decided to remove them from the typical ephemeral being rules and instead have residing in twilight and stuff like that as innate traits. I need to look over Geist's Manifestations over again, but what powers my Wraiths can use that are roughly equivalent to Manifestations in the GMC rules are instead now called <b>Phenomena </b>which I'm thinking will be most miscellaneous Wraith abilities that are somewhat unique to them and not covered by their Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}